course: dictionary
lesson: 7708
title: Words that wound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are slang, and slang can be rude or hurtful even when it sounds funny. Psycho is one of them. Its main slang meaning is a person who is thought to be dangerously crazy or violent, and calling a real person that is unkind.
explain: Context shows you how people use the word. «He went psycho when he lost.» Here psycho means very angry, wild and out of control. Nobody is really dangerous in that sentence. Ask: what word would fit here? Furious would fit, so psycho is a strong, informal way to say someone is very angry.
explain: The example says: «Calling someone a "nerve-disease" case means nutcase or psycho; it mocks people with real illnesses and is not a funny word.» Careful speakers avoid these words, because they hurt people who have real mental illnesses.
fact: Psycho is slang, and as an insult it is rude and offensive.
fact: «Psycho» can mean a person who is thought to be dangerously crazy or violent, as often happens to villains in films and stories.
fact: «He went psycho» is informal slang for being very angry, intense or wild.
fact: The prefix «psycho-» means mind, as in psychology, the study of the mind.
fact: To describe a very angry person kindly, choose a word like furious or wild instead of psycho.
exercise: «He went psycho when he lost the game.» What does psycho mean here? | Sleepy after a long day | Very kind and gentle | *Very angry and wild | Calm and quiet
exercise: In psychology, the prefix psycho- means what? | Animal | Water | *Mind | Fast
exercise: Which is the kindest word to describe a very angry person? | *Furious | Psycho | Loony | Nutcase
test: Why do careful speakers avoid calling someone a psycho? | It is a Scottish word | It is too long to say | It means very happy | *It mocks people with real illnesses
test: Which sentence uses psycho as slang for being very angry? | Ella said the sea was calm. | Ella said the psychologist works at the school. | *Ella said he went psycho when his team lost. | Ella read a book about psychology.
exam: What is the best kind replacement for psycho in «He went psycho when he lost»? | Sleepy | *Furious | Dangerous | Happy
